menu "Denon/Spotify Controller"

menu "Phase 0 spike"

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_SSID
    string "WiFi SSID for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""
    help
        The spike needs a real AP so WiFi DMA contends with the LCD scanout.
        Without it the R1 numbers are optimistic and must not be trusted.
        Environment, not code -- set it here rather than editing main.c.

config DSC_SPIKE_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "WiFi password for the Phase 0 spike"
    default ""

config DSC_SPIKE_URL
    string "HTTPS URL to download repeatedly (with cooldown) during the spike"
    default "https://speed.cloudflare.com/__down?bytes=20971520"
    help
        Cloudflare's speed-test endpoint: size is set by the "bytes" query
        parameter (20 MiB here), no Range header needed, and it exists
        specifically to be hit repeatedly for bandwidth testing -- unlike
        the two hosts tried before it on real hardware:
          - A tiny page (google.com) finishes instantly and measures
            nothing.
          - A public bandwidth-test host on a different provider dropped or
            429'd every connection but the first when hit every ~2 s, and
            even a single request every ~5 s later consistently failed with
            a TLS read error while parsing response headers -- a small
            download from a THIRD host using the identical code path
            succeeded immediately, which ruled out this board's WiFi/TLS
            stack as the cause. Root cause on that host was never
            identified; switched providers instead of continuing to debug
            a specific third party's server behavior.

endmenu

config DSC_FACTORY_TEST
    bool "Build factory test mode instead of the application"
    default n
    help
        Manufacturing hardware exerciser (docs/SECURITY.md §7b). Must never
        be enabled in a shipping build -- tools/check_release.py fails a
        production profile that has this set.

endmenu
